# Task: Survey request control/monitoring on t3 Docker

## Commands
- ssh t3 hostname / docker ps
- Inspect HAProxy cfg, reverse-proxy.sh/yml, UFW, openrouter-proxy

## Findings
- Sole public HTTP(S) front door: haproxy container on :443 (SNI + SSL offload to 127.0.0.1:8443)
- Routes: lexmora, exar, dogan, asip (+ APIs/livekit) via Host header; SoftEther/ovpbackup passthrough
- No HAProxy stats page, access log, rate limit, or deny ACLs in live cfg
- UFW allows 22, 80, 443/tcp+udp, 5201
- Several containers publish host ports (asip-*, dogan-api, exar-api) bypassing HAProxy if reachable
- openrouter-proxy (3proxy) exists for outbound proxy, not ingress control

## Result
Documented current control points and recommended HAProxy-native monitoring/control options.
